    "chunk_text": "Advances in scientific technology have significantly strengthened forensic investigations in Sri Lanka. Sophisticated instruments, such as DNA genetic analyzers, real-time PCR systems, gas chromatography-mass spectrometry (GC-MS), high-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC), comparison microscopes, and advanced digital imaging systems, enable scientists to analyse evidence with remarkable sensitivity and accuracy. These technologies allow investigators to detect evidence that may be invisible to the naked eye.\n\nForensic science benefits society in many ways. It helps identify unknown victims, solve crimes, establish family relationships through DNA testing, prevent wrongful convictions, and strengthen public confidence in the justice system. Every scientific report prepared by a forensic scientist represents countless hours of careful examination and objective analysis aimed at revealing the truth.\n\nAlthough forensic scientists often work behind laboratory doors and remain largely unknown to the public, their contribution to society is invaluable. They combine science, integrity, and impartiality to ensure that justice is based on reliable evidence rather than speculation. As crime becomes increasingly sophisticated, the importance of forensic science will continue to grow, making forensic scientists indispensable guardians of justice in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe views expressed in this article are the author\u2019s own and do not necessarily reflect those of the organisations with which the author is affiliated.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
