    "chunk_text": "Toyota\u2019s flagship showroom in Bambalapitiya breaks ground\n\nToyota Lanka\u2019s growing footprint across Sri Lanka reached another milestone with the groundbreaking ceremony for Toyota\u2019s flagship showroom in Bambalapitiya, held last week.\n\nToyota Sri Lanka Chairman Masaaki Kawabata, Managing Director/CEO Manohara Athukorala, and Chairman of Design Consortium Ltd, Archt. Migara Alwis attended the event\u00a0as special\u00a0invitee.\n\nChairman and Managing Director Manohara Athukorala said that the new showroom represents more than just a facility; it reflects Toyota\u2019s commitment to building stronger relationships, enhancing customer experiences, and delivering world-class service standards. \u201cThis is a long-felt dream that is finally becoming a reality,\u201d he said.\n\nAthukorala recalled that the founding Chairman of Design Consortium, Professor Lakshman, was a valued Toyota customer and maintained a 25-year corporate relationship with the company. \u201cIt is a matter of great pride that his son, Migara, is now designing this flagship showroom,\u201d he said.\n\nDesigned by Design Consortium International, the showroom will feature contemporary architecture focused on innovation and functionality, while offering customers interactive vehicle displays, immersive experiences, and test drives.\n\nUnder the leadership of Archt. Migara Alwis, Design Consortium, and its team continue to demonstrate a strong architectural identity, contributing to the transformation of Colombo\u2019s skyline through innovative and contemporary design.\n\nCSE shifts gears to an energetic session, manufacturing sector performs well\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
