    "chunk_size_bytes": 1922,
    "chunk_text": "Global banking, governance and regulatory to headline Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026\n\nThe Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026, organised by the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLID), will be held on 22 July 2026 at the Cinnamon Grand Colombo under the theme \u201cFuture-Ready Sri Lankan Directors: From Compliance to Sustainable Growth.\u201d\n\nThe Summit will bring together an exceptional gathering of global banking leaders, governance experts, regulators, legal authorities, diplomats, and corporate directors to exchange insights, share international best practices, and explore the evolving role of boards in building resilient, innovative, and sustainable organisations.\n\nThe Summit will feature an outstanding line-up of distinguished speakers, including HSBC Holdings PLC Independent Non-Executive Director and former Chairperson of J.P. Morgan South and Southeast Asia, and recipient of India\u2019s prestigious Padma Shri Award (2024) Kalpana Morparia. She will deliver a keynote address on \u201cThe Changing Role of Bank Directors: From Fiduciary Oversight to Strategic Stewardship,\u201d sharing perspectives from her distinguished career in global banking and board leadership.\n\nJoining her will be two of Sri Lanka\u2019s most respected corporate governance and legal experts\u2014 National Savings Bank and Tokyo Cement Company (Lanka) PLC Chairman Dr. Harsha Cabral, PC and CIC Holdings PLC and Sampath Bank PLC Chairman Harsha Amarasekera, PC.\n\nDr. Cabral, a leading corporate and commercial lawyer and a Chambers Asia-Pacific Band 1 ranked practitioner for Dispute Resolution, will deliver a keynote address titled \u201cBeyond Compliance: How Boards Create Sustainable Value for All Stakeholders.\u201d Drawing on his extensive experience in law, regulation, and board leadership, he will examine how directors can move beyond traditional compliance obligations to become catalysts for long-term value creation."
  },
