    "md5": "e90c9d1c41f013e9fe458bf4db614123",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1614,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka advances regional trade framework with full SLAB digitalisation\n\nSri Lanka receives official invitation to join 5 sponsoring nations for a proposed UN General Assembly resolution\n\nSri Lanka has taken a definitive step towards modernising its national quality infrastructure and expanding its footprint in regional trade through the complete digitalisation of the Sri Lanka Accreditation Board (SLAB).\n\nThe landmark initiative was officially launched during a high-level evening gathering hosted for the Asia Pacific Accreditation Cooperation delegation at The Kingsbury Hotel in Colombo this week.\n\nThe week-long capacity-building programme brought together international experts and delegates from the member economies across the Asia-Pacific region to exchange best practices and elevate technical competencies in conformity assessment.\n\nThe digital transformation, officially inaugurated by Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe, encompasses the automation of all the SLAB accreditation schemes, administrative mechanisms and accounting workflows. Alongside the systemic automation, the SLAB unveiled its newly redesigned official website, engineered to provide a secure, user-friendly digital interface that aligns with the evolving global digital and cybersecurity standards.\n\nThe event, which included key addresses by Ministry Secretary K.A. Vimalenthirarajah and SLAB Acting Director and CEO Chanditha Ediriweera, highlights the state\u2019s strategic focus on leveraging automated compliance frameworks to boost national economic competitiveness."
  },
  {
